Data A Live licensing (repository ShueiTsuki/data-a-live, formerly ios-pandora)

This repository holds two kinds of work under two licences, plus third-party
files that keep their own terms.

1. Kernel changes: Apple Public Source License 2.0 (LICENSES/APSL-2.0.txt)

   - xnu/patches/**  (modifications of Apple's xnu-8796 kernel)
   - the kernel source files under wsl/ that the build copies into the xnu
     tree: wsl/*.c, wsl/*.cpp, wsl/*.h and wsl/*.c.txt

   These modify or extend xnu, which Apple publishes under the APSL 2.0, so
   they are distributed under the same licence. Some patches build on the
   xnu patches of ios-sweet and ios-fuxi; those are modifications of xnu as
   well.

2. Everything else written for this project: MIT (LICENSES/MIT.txt)

   tools/, shim/, the build and test scripts under wsl/ (*.sh, *.py),
   .github/, and the documentation (*.md).

3. Third-party files, under their own licences (their notices are kept next
   to them):

   - wsl/adreno/ArmSmmu4K*.{c,h}: ArmSmmu4K, MIT (wsl/adreno/LICENSE.ArmSmmu4K)
   - wsl/adreno/NativeAdrenoABI.h: NativeAdreno, MIT
     (wsl/adreno/LICENSE.NativeAdreno)
   - tools/native_prelink/: UniXNU, BSD-2-Clause-Patent
     (tools/native_prelink/LICENSE)
   - shim/*/font.h: the 8x16 console font table from ios-sweet's shim
     (generated from the cp850-8x16 PSF console font)

Not in this repository and not covered by any of the above: Apple's iOS
system files (IPSW, dyld shared cache, SDK), Qualcomm and Xiaomi firmware,
and anything read from a phone. The build fetches or expects them separately.

SPDX identifiers: APSL-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause-Patent.
